---
description: Supabase SQL migration and write-boundary safety rules
globs: supabase/**/*.sql
alwaysApply: false
---

# Migration Discipline

- Use additive-only migrations; never rewrite or delete migration history.
- Create migrations with Supabase CLI, not hand-invented filenames.
- Keep function rewrites behavior-equivalent unless behavior change is explicitly approved.
- Preserve ownership/auth checks on every write-boundary function.

# SQL Safety and Contracts

- Prefer SQLSTATE and stable error codes over prose-dependent matching.
- Use `SECURITY DEFINER` only when needed, with `set search_path = ''`.
- Schema-qualify object references in privileged SQL.
- Keep replay/digest/idempotency semantics intact when touching planner write boundaries.

# Coverage and Verification Gate

- Write pgTAP coverage with write-boundary and function changes.
- Regenerate DB types when signatures/columns change (`pnpm types:supabase`)
  as part of the implementation, not as a post-hoc CI chase.
- Do not run `pnpm supabase:reset`, `supabase db lint`, `pnpm test:sql`,
  typecheck, or CI until implementation is done, stacked PRs exist, and the
  user explicitly approves verification.
